    "attribution": "© OpenStreetMap contributors",
    "finding": "Route 1 Haneda southbound stopped at node 579720094 and resumed 1.8 km later at node 36719722. The two OSM ways that carry the carriageway between them opened on 2025-10-29 and are not members of route relation 4256244, and together they exceed the builder's 1 km gap-connector limit. The relation still lists the provisional structure southbound traffic left on that date; it is tagged highway=construction, the builder admitted it as motorway, and in the graph it is a northbound chain that nothing enters or leaves. K3 likewise began from nothing at Honmoku JCT: the one way that feeds it from the Bayshore is outside relation 4259160. Separately, ten interchanges join an exit ramp to an entrance ramp across the surface road they both meet, as one motorway_link chain; seven of those turn traffic back in the opposite direction.",
